    "updated_at": "2021-10-18T13:15:33Z",
    "body": "I'll try a first pass applicability table too. I think the key missing thing from the existing per construct list is distinguishing between whether e.g. they really just mean \"regular attribute\" or \"regular attributes of interfaces/interface mixins only\" (it's usually the latter).\r\n\r\n> The current Default operation kind of implies NewObject, no? This might not always be the case though.\r\n\r\nThe Default toJSON does always \"return a new object\" (`object` type), but [NewObject]-annotated operations are currently required to return \"an interface type or a promise type\".",
